# Lesson 5, new exercise: after 2♦, responder invites with five spades.
title: Five spades, an invitation
id: L05-14
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.3
student: S
board: 29
dealer: N
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KT6    J95    AQJ92  AQ
  E  AJ75   Q843   T87    K9
  S  Q9842  A6     K63    652
  W  3      KT72   54     JT8743

auction:
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C*    = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
     key: 9 points and five spades: start with Stayman.
     not 2S: 2♠ now would be weak, under 8 points. You have 9.
     not 3S: 3♠ would show six spades.
  W Pass
  N 2D     = No 4-card major
  E Pass
  S 2S*    = Five spades, 8-9 points: an invitation
     key: After 2♦, 2♠ shows five spades and invites game.
     not 2NT: Show your five spades first. Partner may have three.
     not 3S: 3♠ here shows 10+ points. You have 9.
  W Pass
  N 4S     = A maximum, with three spades
  E Pass
  S Pass
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Stayman first, then 2♠ showed five spades and 8-9 points. Partner had three
  spades and a maximum, so he bid the game. You are declarer, because you bid
  spades first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 5
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W CJ  N CA  E C9  S C2
  2   N SK  E S5  S S2*  W S3
      S2 key: Dummy's king is winning. Play low.
      S2 not SQ: Did you notice dummy's king already wins this trick? Save your queen.
      note: Draw trumps.
  3   N ST  E S7  S S4  W H2
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   N S6  E SJ  S SQ  W C3
      note: One more round of trumps.
  5   S S9  W D4  N H5  E SA
      note: Trumps are drawn.
  6   E CK  S C5  W C4  N CQ
  7   E HQ  S HA*  W H7  N H9
      HA key: Take the ace now.
      HA not H6: Did you count the defenders' heart tricks? If you duck, they may take two.
  8   S DK  W D5  N D2  E D7
      note: Now the diamonds. Play the king first, the high card from the short side.
  9   S D6  W C7  N DJ  E D8
      note: Over to dummy's diamonds.
  10  N DA  E DT  S D3  W C8
      note: Cash dummy's diamond winners.
  11  N DQ  E H3  S H6  W HT
      note: And the next one.
  12  N D9  E H4  S C6  W CT
      note: The last diamond is a winner too.
  13  N HJ  E H8  S S8  W HK
      note: You ruff the last trick. 11 tricks: 4♠ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, then run dummy's diamonds. Keep your ♠Q when
  dummy's king is winning, and take the ♥A when East leads hearts.

  4♠ made 11 tricks. 3NT would also have made, with nine, so the wrong
  choice would not have cost the game this time. But 4♠ scored more, and the
  5-3 spade fit is usually the better bet.
